---

- `/dungeon generate <id>` · `/dungeon wipe <id>`
- `/dungeon piece <id> <piece>` · `/dungeon pieces <id>`
- `/dungeon reload` · `/dungeon list` · `/dungeon select`
- `/dungeon givekey <id>` · `/dungeon placeportal`
- `/dungeon complete <id>` · `/dungeon return`
- `/dungeon simulate` · `/dungeon event reset` · `/dungeon event resetall`

`simulate` is how you find out a layout never reaches the boss band without wasting twenty keys. `placeportal` is picky about the keystone frame. Try both planes if a command-placed gate will not light.

After you edit packs, `/dungeon reload`, then generate. Check spawn, dead-ends, uniques, and one event marker before you add a second dungeon.
